 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a newly rendered sheet is admitted (2Q policy: first-use queue A1 in FIFO order, reused queue Am in LRU order), the system SHALL place it at the head of A1, evicting before admission: while admission would push A1 over its A1 byte split, the FIFO tail of A1 is evicted.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a request is answered with the cached JPEG for an entry in A1 (requests answered with a pending job ticket do not count), the system SHALL promote the entry to the most-recently-used position of Am.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a request is answered with the cached JPEG for an entry in Am, the system SHALL refresh the entry to the most-recently-used position of Am.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When admission would push total cached JPEG data over budget after A1 is within its A1 byte split, the system SHALL evict the least-recently-used tail of Am before admitting.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: The system SHALL evict only resident sheets; eviction SHALL never delete source footage, cancel pending render jobs, or alter job-ticket semantics, and eviction performed for an admission SHALL not be rolled back if that render later fails.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: The cache shall hold at most 3 GiB in A1 and at most 9 GiB in Am (configured worker parameters, starting values as given), so total cached JPEG data never exceeds the 12 GiB budget.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: When promotion into Am is required while Am is at its Am byte split, the system SHALL evict the least-recently-used tail of Am before promoting.
